S2T (speech-to-text) - local + cloud setup
==========================================

Overview
--------
This project installs and manages an S2T stack with:
- key monitor service (F24 press/release)
- whisper-server user service (model kept in memory)
- cloud ASR support (Google/OpenAI)
- local fallback via whisper-server/whisper-cli
- Ansible-based install/uninstall

Quick start
-----------
1. Prepare tools:
   - ansible-playbook
   - nix
2. Warm up sudo in terminal:
   sudo -v
3. Install:
   make install

Main commands
-------------
- Install:
  make install
- Uninstall:
  make uninstall
- Playbook checks:
  make test-playbooks
- Full tests:
  make test

Services
--------
User services:
- s2t-monitor.service
- s2t-whisper.service

Useful commands:
- List:
  systemctl --user list-units --type=service | rg s2t
- Status:
  systemctl --user status s2t-monitor.service
  systemctl --user status s2t-whisper.service
- Restart:
  systemctl --user restart s2t-monitor.service s2t-whisper.service

Autostart
---------
Autostart is enabled by:
- systemctl --user enable s2t-monitor s2t-whisper
- linger for target user (loginctl enable-linger <user>)

Configuration
-------------
System defaults:
- /etc/s2t/s2t.env

Per-user overrides:
- ~/.config/s2t/s2t.env
- ~/.config/s2t/secrets.env

Current important variables:
- S2T_ASR_PROVIDER=google|openai|google-v2|local
- S2T_USE_SERVER=1
- S2T_NETWORK_ONLY=0|1
- S2T_MAX_RESPONSE_SECONDS=5
- S2T_GOOGLE_TIMEOUT_SEC=4
- S2T_MODEL_PATH=/home/<user>/.local/share/s2t/ggml-*.bin

ASR behavior
------------
- Cloud-first:
  set S2T_ASR_PROVIDER to google/openai/google-v2.
- Local fallback enabled:
  S2T_NETWORK_ONLY=0
- Strict cloud-only (no local fallback):
  S2T_NETWORK_ONLY=1

Logs
----
- Runtime log:
  /run/user/$(id -u)/s2t/s2t.log
- Monitor journal:
  journalctl --user -u s2t-monitor.service -f
- Whisper journal:
  journalctl --user -u s2t-whisper.service -f

Log growth control is handled by controller variables:
- S2T_LOG_MAX_BYTES
- S2T_LOG_KEEP
- S2T_WHISPER_ARTIFACT_KEEP
- S2T_WHISPER_LOG_MAX_BYTES

Resource limits (systemd cgroups)
---------------------------------
Configured in user units:
- s2t-whisper.service:
  CPUQuota=350%
  MemoryHigh=2500M
  MemoryMax=3G
  TasksMax=64
- s2t-monitor.service:
  CPUQuota=50%
  MemoryMax=256M
  TasksMax=32

Troubleshooting
---------------
If install fails on sudo in non-interactive mode:
1. Run:
   sudo -v
2. Run install again:
   make install

If cloud ASR is slow/unavailable:
1. Check runtime log for provider timing and fallback.
2. Verify provider keys/credentials in secrets file.
3. Set S2T_NETWORK_ONLY according to expected behavior.
